{
  "_comment": [
    "Plain-text source for the secure.config shipped to the warewolfserver-uat",
    "Cloud test Function App by Dev/.azure/pipeline-CLOUD.yml.",
    "",
    "The pipeline's Build stage encrypts this JSON with",
    "Dev2.Services.Security.SecurityEncryption.Encrypt (the same AES-CBC routine",
    "the Warewolf Studio uses) and writes the result to the publish output as",
    "'secure.config'. SecureConfigLoader reads it from AppContext.BaseDirectory",
    "at runtime; without it the engine has no effective permission map and",
    "WorkflowAuthPolicyLoader denies every request with 503 ConfigMissing.",
    "",
    "SecretKey is intentionally empty: SecureConfigLoader synthesises an",
    "in-memory HMAC key when it is blank, so no secret is committed here.",
    "",
    "Public has no server-wide grant: 'Hello World' is the only workflow anyone",
    "can view or run anonymously (its resource-scoped Public row below).",
    "",
    "Warewolf_ClientApps is the app-role granted to app-only client apps (e.g.",
    "the AzureFunction / ServiceBus client examples' Managed Identities) by",
    "Configure-WwExecutionAuth-Clients.ps1 -AppRolesToAssign. Its per-workflow",
    "row below (IsServer=false, matched case-insensitively on ResourceName)",
    "lets those clients View+Execute 'Hello World' via /secure/. The WindowsGroup",
    "value must equal the sanitized Entra app-role value in the token's roles",
    "claim; ResourceID is not used for matching, so it stays a zero GUID.",
    "",
    "'Authenticated Users' is an implicit role every signed-in (delegated) Entra",
    "caller holds (WorkflowClaimsPrincipal.AuthenticatedUsersGroup); anonymous and",
    "app-only callers do not. It gives the Web Studio's users View server-wide and",
    "nothing else: no Execute and no Contribute. warewolfserver's WAREWOLF_ENTRA_CONFIG",
    "uses tenantId 'common', so any Microsoft account (any organization, or personal)",
    "is an Authenticated User here.",
    "",
    "ashley.lewis@theunlimited.co.za is a direct UPN entry (WorkflowPolicyMatcher",
    "matches a row's WindowsGroup against the caller's UPN): View, Execute and",
    "Contribute server-wide, so she can create and run workflows.",
    "",
    "The sources that existed on warewolfserver on 2026-10-31 (Azure Exchange Source,",
    "Local Server Source, NewSqlServerSource, Warewolf DevOps RabbitMQ Source) each have",
    "resource-scoped rows below, so Authenticated Users can't view them. A resource row",
    "replaces the whole global map for that resource, so each also needs its own",
    "Warewolf Administrators row, and Public gets nothing on them.",
    "",
    "'Hello World' has resource-scoped rows (below): once a workflow has ANY",
    "resource-specific (IsServer=false) entry, the global role map is discarded",
    "entirely for that workflow (WorkflowAuthPolicyLoader 'resource scope takes",
    "priority' rule, WOLF-8418 - see WorkflowPolicyMatcher.cs). Its Public row is",
    "what makes the anonymous /Public/Hello World.json smoke test work."
  ],
